vsm2.20:97.11:
“(1) He sees the fall of the feeling aggregate in the sense of conditioned cessation thus: With the cessation of ignorance there
is the cessation of feeling; (2) … with the cessation of craving … (3) … with the cessation of kamma … (4) he sees the fall of the
feeling aggregate in the sense of conditioned cessation thus: With the cessation of contact there is the cessation of feeling;
